<article class="env-lemma" id="0A26">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A26">Lemma <span data-tag="0A26">33.43.4</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a proper scheme over a field $k$. If $\dim (X) \leq 1$ then $X$ is H-projective over $k$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0A25" data-tag="0A25">33.43.3</a> we see that $X$ is a locally closed subscheme of $\mathbf{P}^ n_ k$ for some field $k$. Since $X$ is proper over $k$ it follows that $X$ is a closed subscheme of $\mathbf{P}^ n_ k$ (Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01W6" data-tag="01W6">29.42.7</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>